akr 0.1
project legeos

record legeos.papercut.adr-0012-landed-as-a-markdown-adr-without-a/1 : papercut {
    title "ADR-0012 landed as a markdown ADR without a matching ledger record, so…"
    state verified
    statement """
        ADR-0012 landed as a markdown ADR without a matching ledger record, so for several commits the ledger kept asserting cosmic-comp was a pinned fork (D6) and cosmic-greeter the greeter (D10), both active, while the tree said otherwise. Nothing flagged it — a decision recorded only in docs/adr/ is invisible to validation. Worth a check that every docs/adr/NNNN-*.md has a corresponding decision record.
        """
    observed_at git:4ad95f78386d93a93e6fa500c43661908e00a658
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-21
}

record legeos.papercut.bumping-interfaces-wayland-lege-shell-v1-xml-to/1 : papercut {
    title "Bumping interfaces/wayland/lege-shell-v1.xml to version 2: `cargo xtask…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Bumping interfaces/wayland/lege-shell-v1.xml to version 2: `cargo xtask check-interfaces` only covers interfaces/dbus/, so drift between the Wayland XML and the two generated modules (compositor protocols.rs, shell protocol.rs) is caught only by a compile failure, and a `since` added to the XML without a version guard at the send site would not be caught at all. A small xtask arm that checks each interface's declared version against the compositor's create_global and the shell's bind would close this.
        """
    observed_at git:70df99e539de1899ef5740db2456504a906a16ad
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-22
}

record legeos.papercut.partitioning-file-ownership-across-five/1 : papercut {
    title "Partitioning file ownership across five parallel agents left the shared…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Partitioning file ownership across five parallel agents left the shared vocabulary crates (lege-types, lege-client/src/proxies) owned by nobody, so a cross-cutting contract could not be added by anyone: the checkpoint protocol was documented and implemented on both ends but had no wire transport, and the session daemon correctly reported it was barred from adding one. Whoever partitions parallel work should own the shared vocabulary themselves and settle cross-cutting contracts up front, as was done for org.legeos.Resources1 — that one worked precisely because it was fixed before the agents started.
        """
    observed_at git:b543668447e5e95a089b70cd971624abb77cab19
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-21
}

record legeos.papercut.promoting-decisions-to-active-with-akr-revise/1 : papercut {
    title "Promoting decisions to active with `akr revise <key> --state active` in…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Promoting decisions to active with `akr revise <key> --state active` in text mode printed only "nothing written" — the actual reason (V-021: active decision cites nothing; and V-005: supported_by may not target a constraint, use implements) only appeared with --format json. Text mode should print the blocking diagnostics too.
        """
    observed_at git:595f75f325e764e25b0befc39b6286e2a0e77f27
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-17
}
